// 3. Staircase search: rows and columns sorted ascending, O(m + n).
static boolean staircase(int[][] matrix, int target) {
    int r = 0, c = matrix[0].length - 1;
    while (r < matrix.length && c >= 0) {
        int v = matrix[r][c];
        if (v == target) return true;
        if (v > target) c--; // everything below in this column is larger
        else r++;            // everything left in this row is smaller
    }
    return false;
}
```

Snippet 1 compares cells with `'1'`, keeps marks in a separate `boolean[][]` so the caller's board is untouched, and uses an explicit stack, so it never throws `StackOverflowError` on a 1,000 × 1,000 grid.

