```java
// 3. Dijkstra: adj.get(u) holds {v, weight} pairs with weight >= 0.
static int[] dijkstra(List<List<int[]>> adj, int source) {
    int[] dist = new int[adj.size()];
    Arrays.fill(dist, Integer.MAX_VALUE);
    dist[source] = 0;
    PriorityQueue<int[]> heap = new PriorityQueue<>((a, b) -> Integer.compare(a[0], b[0])); // {distance, node}
    heap.offer(new int[] {0, source});
    while (!heap.isEmpty()) {
        int[] top = heap.poll();
        int d = top[0], u = top[1];
        if (d > dist[u]) continue; // stale entry: a shorter path was found after it was offered
        for (int[] e : adj.get(u)) {
            int v = e[0], nd = d + e[1];
            if (nd < dist[v]) {
                dist[v] = nd;
                heap.offer(new int[] {nd, v});
            }
        }
    }
    return dist;
}
```

Snippet 3 skips stale entries instead of updating them because `PriorityQueue` has no decrease-key; `remove(Object)` would work but costs O(n) per update.

