Java · Java Linked Lists · Doubly linked, circular and java.util.LinkedList track
Two snippets cover the hand-built doubly linked list and the library's cursor.

```java
// 1. Doubly linked list with sentinels: the core of an LRU cache.
final class DoublyLinkedList {
    static final class Node {
        int key, val;
        Node prev, next;
        Node(int key, int val) { this.key = key; this.val = val; }
    }

    private final Node head = new Node(0, 0), tail = new Node(0, 0); // sentinels

    DoublyLinkedList() {
        head.next = tail;
        tail.prev = head;
    }

    void addFirst(Node n) {
        n.prev = head;
        n.next = head.next;
        head.next.prev = n;
        head.next = n;
    }

    void unlink(Node n) {
        n.prev.next = n.next;
        n.next.prev = n.prev;
        n.prev = n.next = null; // detach fully
    }

    Node removeLast() {
        if (tail.prev == head) return null; // empty
        Node n = tail.prev;
        unlink(n);
        return n;
    }
}

// 2. ListIterator: O(1) removal and insertion at the cursor of a java.util.LinkedList.
List<Integer> list = new LinkedList<>(List.of(1, 2, 3, 4));
for (ListIterator<Integer> it = list.listIterator(); it.hasNext(); ) {
    int x = it.next();
    if (x % 2 == 0) it.remove(); // removes the element just returned
    else it.add(x * 10);         // inserts right after it
}
// list is now [1, 10, 3, 30]
```

Snippet 1 plus a `HashMap` from key to node is the hand-written LRU Cache that interviewers often ask for after a learner reaches for `LinkedHashMap`; both appear in the Java maps blueprint's curriculum.

