Concept: BitSet stores dense non-negative integers in one bit each; count members with cardinality
Misconception: bitSet.size() returns the number of members.
Explanation: BitSet is a growable array of bits indexed by non-negative ints, far smaller than a HashSet<Integer> for dense ranges. set, get and clear work on single bits; and, or, xor and andNot combine whole sets. size() is the number of bits of storage (a multiple of 64), not the number of members; cardinality() counts the set bits. Walk members with nextSetBit.
Incorrect:
