// 3. Meeting Rooms II as a sweep over a TreeMap difference map.
static int minMeetingRooms(int[][] intervals) {
    TreeMap<Integer, Integer> delta = new TreeMap<>();
    for (int[] m : intervals) {
        delta.merge(m[0], 1, Integer::sum);  // a meeting starts
        delta.merge(m[1], -1, Integer::sum); // a meeting ends; same-time end and start cancel out
    }
    int rooms = 0, best = 0;
    for (int d : delta.values()) { // values in key (time) order
        rooms += d;
        best = Math.max(best, rooms);
    }
    return best;
}
```

Snippet 2 is Time Based Key-Value Store (NeetCode 150): with `floorEntry` it is a few lines, while in JavaScript it needs a hand-written binary search over each key's history.

