The compression-plus-Fenwick combination in Java:

```java
// Count of Smaller Numbers After Self: compress values to ranks, then sweep right to left.
static List<Integer> countSmaller(int[] nums) {
    int[] sorted = Arrays.stream(nums).distinct().sorted().toArray(); // ranks 0..k-1
    Fenwick fenwick = new Fenwick(sorted.length);
    Integer[] res = new Integer[nums.length];
    for (int i = nums.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        int rank = Arrays.binarySearch(sorted, nums[i]);
        res[i] = (int) fenwick.prefix(rank - 1); // strictly smaller values already seen on the right
        fenwick.add(rank, 1);
    }
    return Arrays.asList(res);
}
```

The snippet uses the `Fenwick` class from section 2, whose `prefix(-1)` returns 0, so the smallest value needs no special case.

