Concept: Set.add returns false when the element is already present
Misconception: Detecting a duplicate needs a contains check followed by an add.
Explanation: Set.add returns true when it inserted the element and false when an equal element was already there. One call therefore both tests and records membership. This makes duplicate detection a single line and lets BFS mark nodes as visited at the moment they are queued: if (visited.add(next)) queue.add(next). JavaScript's Set.add returns the set instead, so this idiom has no direct JavaScript equivalent.
