Concept: Declare stacks as Deque and implement them with ArrayDeque
Misconception: java.util.Stack is the standard Java stack.
Explanation: Stack is a legacy class that extends Vector: every method is synchronized, it exposes index access such as get(0), and it iterates from bottom to top. The Java documentation recommends the Deque interface instead. ArrayDeque is faster, its push, pop and peek all work at the head, and it iterates from top to bottom. It rejects null elements.
