node = node.next[word.charAt(i) - 'a']; // throws for 'A', '3' or 'é'; NPE later if the slot is null
Correct:
static int index(char ch) {
  char lower = Character.toLowerCase(ch);
  if (lower < 'a' || lower > 'z') throw new IllegalArgumentException("unsupported: " + ch);
  return lower - 'a';
}
Complexity: O(1) per step; 26 references per node

