        for (int i = 0; i < word.length(); i++) {
            int c = word.charAt(i) - 'a';
            Node child = node.next[c];
            if (--child.pass == 0) { // only this word used the branch: drop it whole
                node.next[c] = null;
                return true;
            }
            node = child;
        }
        node.end = false;
        return true;
    }
}
```

The class assumes lowercase input, as Implement Trie guarantees; a production version would validate or normalise each character before indexing, or switch to map children.

