```javascript
// 3. Staircase search: rows and columns sorted ascending, O(m + n).
function staircase(matrix, target) {
  let r = 0, c = matrix[0].length - 1;
  while (r < matrix.length && c >= 0) {
    const v = matrix[r][c];
    if (v === target) return true;
    if (v > target) c--; // everything below in this column is larger
    else r++;            // everything left in this row is smaller
  }
  return false;
}
```

Snippet 1 uses a flat `Uint8Array` for the seen marks, which avoids both mutating the caller's grid and the string keys a Set would need; it also shows why recursion is the wrong default on a 1,000 × 1,000 grid.

