Concept: A max-heap and a min-heap split a stream into lower and upper halves
Misconception: A running median needs the whole stream kept sorted.
Explanation: The median only depends on the middle of the data. Keep the lower half in a max-heap and the upper half in a min-heap, with every lower value no larger than every upper value and the lower half equal in size or one larger. Each new value goes into the lower heap, its maximum moves to the upper heap, and if the upper heap becomes larger its minimum moves back. The median is the lower top, or the average of both tops.
Incorrect:
// O(n) insert per value: splicing into a sorted array.
const i = sorted.findIndex(v => v > x);
sorted.splice(i === -1 ? sorted.length : i, 0, x);
Correct:
class MedianFinder {
  #low = new Heap((a, b) => b - a);
  #high = new Heap((a, b) => a - b);
  addNum(x) {
    this.#low.push(x);
    this.#high.push(this.#low.pop());
    if (this.#high.size > this.#low.size) this.#low.push(this.#high.pop());
  }
  findMedian() {
    return this.#low.size > this.#high.size
      ? this.#low.peek()
      : (this.#low.peek() + this.#high.peek()) / 2;
  }
}
