Concept: Save the next reference before rewiring a node
Misconception: The order of the assignments in a reversal loop does not matter.
Explanation: A node's next reference is the only way to reach the rest of the list. Overwriting it before saving it in a variable loses every node after it. Save next, rewire, then advance, in that order.
