Concept: Two pointers kept n nodes apart find the nth node from the end in one pass
Misconception: Removing the nth node from the end needs one pass to count the length and a second to remove.
Explanation: Move a lead pointer n + 1 steps ahead of a trail pointer, starting both at a dummy node, then move them together until lead is null. trail then sits just before the node to remove. The dummy covers the case where the head itself is removed, which otherwise needs its own branch.
Incorrect:
let lead = head, trail = head;
for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) lead = lead.next;
while (lead.next) { lead = lead.next; trail = trail.next; } // TypeError when n equals the length
trail.next = trail.next.next;
Correct:
function removeNthFromEnd(head, n) {
  const dummy = new ListNode(0, head);
  let lead = dummy, trail = dummy;
  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) lead = lead.next; // lead is n + 1 nodes ahead
  while (lead) { lead = lead.next; trail = trail.next; }
  trail.next = trail.next.next;
  return dummy.next;
}
Complexity: O(n) time, O(1) space, one pass

