JavaScript · linked_list · patterns · L4
Concept: Harder list problems combine three moves, finding the middle, reversing a half and merging
Misconception: Reorder List needs an array of nodes or recursion.
Explanation: Reorder List, Palindrome Linked List and similar problems split into steps already learned. Find the middle with fast and slow pointers, cut the list there, reverse the second half with the save-next loop, then weave or compare the two halves. Each step is O(n) time and O(1) space, so the whole solution is too. An array of nodes also works, but it costs O(n) extra memory.
Incorrect:
const nodes = [];
for (let n = head; n; n = n.next) nodes.push(n); // O(n) extra memory
Correct:
function reorderList(head) {
  if (!head) return;
  let slow = head, fast = head;
  while (fast.next && fast.next.next) { slow = slow.next; fast = fast.next.next; }
  let prev = null, curr = slow.next;
  slow.next = null;                                  // cut after the middle
  while (curr) { const next = curr.next; curr.next = prev; prev = curr; curr = next; }
  let a = head, b = prev;                            // weave the halves
  while (b) {
    const an = a.next, bn = b.next;
    a.next = b; b.next = an;
    a = an; b = bn;
  }
}
Complexity: O(n) time, O(1) space

