JavaScript · object · fit-and-alternatives · L2
Concept: A {} dictionary inherits keys such as constructor and __proto__, so use Object.create(null) or a Map
Misconception: An empty object literal has no keys, so if (dict[word]) is a safe membership test.
Explanation: {} inherits from Object.prototype, so dict['constructor'] and dict['toString'] are functions, and assigning dict['__proto__'] changes the prototype instead of storing a value. Words taken from input can hit these names. Object.create(null) makes a dictionary with no inherited keys, Object.hasOwn checks only own keys, and a Map avoids the problem entirely.
