Explanation: a.filter(x => b.includes(x)) is O(n * m). Iterate the smaller set and keep the values the larger set has, which is O(min(n, m)). Union is new Set([...a, ...b]), and difference keeps the values of a that b lacks. Node 22 and current browsers also have a.intersection(b), a.union(b) and a.difference(b), which return new sets, but check the judge's runtime before relying on them.
