Concept: A monotonic stack of indexes finds every next greater element in one O(n) pass
Misconception: Finding the next greater element for every position needs a nested loop.
Explanation: Keep a stack of indexes whose answer is still unknown, with their values decreasing from bottom to top. When a larger value arrives, it is the answer for every smaller value on top, so pop them and record it. Each index is pushed and popped once, so the whole pass is O(n). Store indexes rather than values when the answer is a distance.
