Concept: Walk a list with while (curr), and check a pointer before reading its next
Misconception: while (curr.next) visits every node in the list.
Explanation: while (curr.next) stops at the last node without processing it, and throws on an empty list because reading next from null is a TypeError. while (curr) visits every node, including the last, and handles a null head. A fast pointer that jumps two nodes must check fast && fast.next before each jump.
