Concept: A dummy node before the head removes the special case for the first node
Misconception: Code that builds or edits a list needs a separate branch for the first node.
Explanation: When the head itself may be removed, or the result list starts empty, start from const dummy = new ListNode(0, head) and keep a tail or prev pointer. Every node, including the first, then has a node before it, so one rule handles every position. Return dummy.next at the end.
Incorrect:
