Explanation: All three recurse into the left subtree and then the right. Preorder visits the node before its children, inorder between them and postorder after them. Preorder copies or serialises a tree, inorder lists a BST in sorted order, and postorder computes answers that need both children first, such as height. Push into one shared result array instead of concatenating arrays at every level.
