Concept: An explicit stack replaces recursion; push the right child before the left for preorder
Misconception: Iterative preorder pushes the left child and then the right child.
Explanation: A stack pops the last item pushed, so preorder pushes the right child first to process the left one first. Inorder walks left while pushing each node, then pops a node, visits it and moves to its right child. Iteration avoids the call-stack limit on very deep, skewed trees, which in Node is often around ten thousand frames.
