Concept: Start a new traversal from every node not yet seen, because one traversal covers only one component
Misconception: A DFS from node 0 visits the whole graph.
Explanation: A traversal reaches only the nodes connected to where it starts. Graphs in interview problems are often disconnected, so wrap the traversal in an outer loop over every node and start a new one from each node not yet seen. The number of starts is the number of components, and the whole loop is still O(V + E) because each node is visited once.
Incorrect:
function countComponents(n, edges) {
  const adj = buildGraph(n, edges);
  dfs(adj, 0);
  return 1; // nodes not connected to 0 are never visited or counted
}
Correct:
function countComponents(n, edges) {
  const adj = Array.from({ length: n }, () => []);
  for (const [a, b] of edges) { adj[a].push(b); adj[b].push(a); }
  const seen = new Array(n).fill(false);
  let count = 0;
  for (let s = 0; s < n; s++) {
    if (seen[s]) continue;
    count++;
    const stack = [s];
    seen[s] = true;
    while (stack.length) {
      const u = stack.pop();
      for (const v of adj[u]) if (!seen[v]) { seen[v] = true; stack.push(v); }
    }
  }
  return count;
}
Complexity: O(V + E) time, O(V) space

