Concept: Map keys match by SameValueZero, not by contents
Misconception: Two arrays or objects with the same contents are the same Map key.
Explanation: Map compares keys with SameValueZero: primitives by value (NaN equals NaN, 0 equals -0), objects and arrays only by reference. Each array literal is a new object, so a key built from [r, c] never matches a later [r, c]. Encode composite keys as strings or nest Maps.
