JavaScript · union_find · patterns · L4
Concept: Store each node's ratio to its parent, and combine ratios along the path
Misconception: Ratio questions such as a / c from a / b and b / c need a graph search per query.
Explanation: Weighted union-find keeps weight(x) = value(x) / value(parent(x)). During find, after the parent has been compressed, multiply x's weight by its parent's weight, so x points straight at the root with the correct ratio. To union a / b = ratio, link a's root under b's root with weight ratio * weight(b) / weight(a). Two variables with the same root answer a / b as weight(a) / weight(b); different roots mean the answer is unknown.
Incorrect:
weight.set(x, weight.get(x) * weight.get(p)); // before find(p): p's weight is not yet relative to the root
parent.set(x, find(p));
Correct:
class RatioUnionFind {
  #parent = new Map();
  #weight = new Map(); // value(x) = weight(x) * value(parent(x))
  #add(x) {
    if (!this.#parent.has(x)) { this.#parent.set(x, x); this.#weight.set(x, 1); }
  }
  #find(x) {
    const p = this.#parent.get(x);
    if (p !== x) {
      const root = this.#find(p);
      this.#weight.set(x, this.#weight.get(x) * this.#weight.get(p));
      this.#parent.set(x, root);
    }
    return this.#parent.get(x);
  }
  union(a, b, ratio) { // a / b = ratio
    this.#add(a);
    this.#add(b);
    const ra = this.#find(a), rb = this.#find(b);
    if (ra === rb) return;
    this.#parent.set(ra, rb);
    this.#weight.set(ra, ratio * this.#weight.get(b) / this.#weight.get(a));
  }
  query(a, b) {
    if (!this.#parent.has(a) || !this.#parent.has(b)) return -1;
    if (this.#find(a) !== this.#find(b)) return -1;
    return this.#weight.get(a) / this.#weight.get(b);
  }
}
Complexity: Nearly O(1) amortised per operation

