Concept: Three-way partition sorts values 0, 1 and 2 in one pass with three pointers
Misconception: After swapping with the high pointer, advance the middle pointer like any other swap.
Explanation: Keep low (next slot for 0), mid (current), high (next slot for 2). If a[mid] is 0, swap with low and advance both; if 1, advance mid; if 2, swap with high and shrink high but do not advance mid, because the element that arrived from high has not been examined. One pass, O(n) time, O(1) space. The same partition handles less-than, equal-to and greater-than a pivot, which is how quicksort copes with many duplicates.
Incorrect:
