Concept: Use amount + 1 as the unreachable sentinel, because Integer.MAX_VALUE + 1 wraps negative
Misconception: Integer.MAX_VALUE is a safe "infinity" for a minimum, as Infinity is in JavaScript.
Explanation: dp[a] is the fewest coins that make amount a. Unreachable cells need a value that never wins a min. Java has no Infinity for int, and Integer.MAX_VALUE + 1 wraps to Integer.MIN_VALUE, which then wins every min. Any real answer is at most amount (all 1-coins), so amount + 1 is a safe sentinel that cannot overflow. After the loops return -1 when dp[amount] is still amount + 1. Loop amounts outside and coins inside.
